T = 200°C = 473 K. Using the thermal Doppler FWHM:

\[
\Delta \nu_D=\frac{c}{\lambda}\sqrt{\frac{8kT\ln2}{m_H c^2}}
=\frac{\sqrt{8kT\ln2/m_H}}{\lambda}
\]

With \(m_H\approx1.67\times10^{-27}\) kg and \(\lambda=6563\) Å:

\[
\Delta \nu_D \approx 7.17\times10^9\text{ Hz}
\]

\[
\Delta \lambda_D=\lambda\frac{\Delta \nu_D}{\nu_0}\approx0.103\ \text{Å}
\]

Answer: C

For two masses connected by a spring, use the reduced mass:

\[
\mu=\frac{m_1m_2}{m_1+m_2}
=\frac{(0.1)(0.2)}{0.1+0.2}
=\frac{0.02}{0.3}
=\frac{1}{15}\text{ kg}
\]

Angular frequency:

\[
\omega=\sqrt{\frac{k}{\mu}}
=\sqrt{\frac{0.5}{1/15}}
=\sqrt{7.5}
\approx 2.74\ \text{rad s}^{-1}
\]

Answer: H
